<title>UK: LME copper probes $1,950 barrier in late trading.</title>
<headline>LME copper probes $1,950 barrier in late trading.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>LME copper strolled higher in late inter-office trading, gently probing the $1,950 barrier. At 1800 GMT, three months copper was indicated at $1,947/51, up from the kerb close of $1,940 per tonne.</p>
<p>This week, copper has repeatedly confronted $1,950 resistance, aided by healthy stock reductions, but failed to sustain any move above that area.</p>
<p>The other metals were barely changed.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 8065</p>
